::: {.doc-subject}

Get a tabular report of the checks of the synthetic data.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/posit-dev/pointblank/blob/main/pointblank/synthetic.py#L513-L737){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}
```pythonsignature
SyntheticCheck.get_tabular_report(
    title=None,
    lang=None,
    locale=None,
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

The report has a group of rows for each check: the fidelity of each column, the
diversity of the rows and of the text, and the copies of seed rows. Each row has a badge
with its result, and the header says how many issues there are.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[title]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   An optional title replacing the default.

<code>[lang]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The language of the report's text, as a two-letter language code (e.g., `"fr"` or
    `"de"`; see the `lang=` argument of [`Validate`](`pointblank.Validate`) for the
    languages). By default, the report is in English. The names of the columns are shown
    as they are.

<code>[locale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The locale for the numbers in the report (e.g., `"de-CH"`), which sets the decimal
    mark and the thousands separator. By default, it's `lang=`.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [GT]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A Great Tables object.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#30fc1bb9 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import pointblank as pb
import polars as pl

seed = pl.DataFrame({"x": list(range(100)), "y": ["a", "b"] * 50})
synthetic = pl.DataFrame({"x": [k % 10 for k in range(100)], "y": ["a", "b"] * 50})

pb.check_synthetic(synthetic, seed).get_tabular_report()
```

